governor and may be removed by the governor as provided in
W.S. 9-1-202. The director shall:
(vi) Consult the governor and assist the
attorney general and division of criminal investigation on
the designation of critical infrastructure zones and the
investigation and identification of conveyances, leases and
leasehold interests within as defined by W.S.
19-13-501(a)(i), located up to five (5) miles of from
critical infrastructure zones as disclosed by the
recordings reported by county clerks in accordance with
W.S. 19-13-501 and 19-13-502.
19-13-105. Homeland security program.
(e) The office of homeland security may receive and
share criminal identification, intelligence and criminal
history information available to law enforcement agencies
for the purposes provided by W.S. 19-13-103.
19-13-501. Definitions.
(a) As used in this article:
(i) "Conveyance" means as defined by W.S.
34-1-102 and includes conveyances of every instrument in
writing by which any interest in real property, surface
interests, mineral interests and pore space interests is
created, alienated, mortgaged, leased or assigned, or by
which the title to any real property may be affected in law
or in equity. "Conveyance" shall not include wills;
(iv) "Designated country or person" means:
3

